{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbbPCSR4uVXmhR4XLHbN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `block_rhythm_regularity` and it passes the self-check: it prints `OK` and the data contract holds. The check doesn't test novelty against the other models, convergence on a full fit, or the 30-minute time limit, so none of those are known yet.\n\n**What I refined:** the incumbent `run_length_variety_preference`. In that model, strict alternation (HTHTHTHT, where every run is a single flip) has the lowest possible run-length variety, so it gets the biggest \"designed rhythm\" penalty. That pushes against the critique's one finding (q≈0.08, so it misses the usual 0.05 cutoff): among two highly alternating sequences, people pick the more alternating one more often than the model predicts.\n\n**The one change:** the rhythm penalty now applies only to repeated blocks of identical flips, like HHTTHHTT or HHHTTTHH. It is the lack of run-length variety multiplied by the share of flips that sit in runs of two or more. Strict alternation therefore gets no rhythm penalty and is judged only against each person's own ideal switching rate. Everything else is the incumbent's, unchanged.\n\nI didn't graft in the asymmetric ideal-rate penalty, the obvious fix for this critique. The ledger shows it has already been tried three times, and the best of those (rank 1) lost to the incumbent.\n\n**Self-check numbers:** the 100-draw, single-chain smoke fit gave an ELPD-LOO of -2262.3, against the incumbent's -2272.9. That is encouraging but not a fair comparison, because the smoke fit is far shorter than a production fit. The check also flagged PSIS-LOO as unreliable on that fit (7.9% of trials have a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance), so the -2262.3 itself may be off.\n\nFiles are in `iter_4/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4004,"cache_read_input_tokens":80576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4004,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90947548-97d5-4154-a57c-65df7dcc068c","uuid":"671d494d-7591-4c0d-b925-0a71fd037ad5","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:26:41.532Z","request_id":"req_011CfbbPBohi8aPpvc7kuYN8"}
